  "_meta": {
    "version": "v0.2.0-pre.7",
    "supersedes": "v0.1.1",
    "relationship": "Vocabulary v0.2 — first-class Warrant/Artifact/SourceFragment/EvidenceBinding/ConfidenceRecord/AccessScope/AILineage/RetentionPolicy/MappingState/Workspace primitives; OA/PROV-O/SKOS/ELI predicate-level imports; AKN/USLM/DPV/ODRL alignments; legacy v0.1 ontology aspirations demoted per the §9 four-mode reshape (PKA-03og). v0.1.x is editorial baseline only — wholesale supersession.",
    "delta_from_v0.1": [
      "Added rkaf:definedInScope as @type:@id (was missing, treated as string literal in v0.1)",
      "Added rkaf:Artifact, rkaf:SourceFragment, rkaf:EvidenceBinding, rkaf:Warrant, rkaf:ConfidenceRecord, rkaf:AccessScope as first-class primitives",
      "Added rkaf:hasWarrant universal grounding predicate (rkaf:hasAuthority becomes legal-family specialization)",
      "Added rkaf:AILineage; rkaf:humanApprover is OPTIONAL as of the v0.2 provenance-role split — an unreviewed model candidate must be representable, and approval is an rkaf:Attestation (spec/rkaf-core.md §2.4)",
      "Added Artifact and SourceFragment identity bindings: rkaf:hasContentDigest, rkaf:versionLineageEvidence, rkaf:sourceArtifactDigest, rkaf:fragmentContentDigest, rkaf:coordinateSystem, and the OA offset predicates oa:start / oa:end",
      "Added rkaf:ConceptScheme and evidence-bearing rkaf:ConceptAssignment, with skos:inScheme, skos:definition, and skos:hasTopConcept as mode-1 SKOS imports",
      "Added the document-analysis module (spec/rkaf-analysis.md): rkaf:RelationChangeEvent, rkaf:RelationComparisonContext, rkaf:ResolverProofIssuer, rkaf:ResolverProofRecord, and the neutral rkaf:RelationFinding. Generic and jurisdiction-free; the kernel does not depend on them, profiles may.",
      "Added rkaf:ClosureClaim as EXPERIMENTAL AND DISABLED: rkaf:closureClaimStatus is closed over the single value rkaf:closureClaimDisabled, no finding may cite a ClosureClaim, and no omission finding kind exists (spec/rkaf-analysis.md 6)",
      "Added rkaf:MappingState, rkaf:RetentionPolicy, rkaf:Workspace, rkaf:projectsTo, rkaf:llmHint (Studio-derived promotions)",
      "Added rkaf:anchoredBy / rkaf:anchorType (abstract anchoring contract, bindings live outside Rulespec)",
      "Mode-1 direct predicate imports: prov:, oa:, skos:, eli:, foaf:primaryTopic, the DCAT qualified-relation quartet, dcterms:hasFormat, dcterms:isFormatOf, and dcterms:relation (§9.1). All carry term defs in this context.",
      "Mode-2/3 alignments (class-tag and URI-value composition): aknt:, uslm:, dpv:, odrl: (§9.2). External prefix declared; rkaf-namespaced predicates carry the external IRIs as values.",
      "See also (future-projection, no predicate import): lrml:, rrmv:, eco:, sepio:, cito:, and the unimported dcterms supersession predicates (§9.2.2). Promote to §9.2 Alignment when a partner consumer arrives with a named use case.",
      "Reintroduced dcat: for the Experimental rulemaking module's named Spicy Regs carrier: dcat:qualifiedRelation, dcat:Relationship, and dcat:hadRole now have executable corpus and fixture coverage.",
      "Dropped remaining Cohort D dead-weight prefix declarations: nano: (pattern citation, not predicate import) and schemaorg: (no SEO projector). Re-declare when the dependent layer ships.",
      "Retained the legacy hasProceedingEvidenceIdentifier context aliases for Experimental pre-release decoding; they no longer occur in the current Proceeding shape.",
      "Completeness sweep: every class a CUE shape binds now carries a term definition here. The reshape added rkaf:ValueAssertion, rkaf:SourceClaimant, rkaf:ExtractionActivity, oa:TextQuoteSelector, and oa:TextPositionSelector as compiled, schema-bound classes without one; rkaf:Assertion and rkaf:RelationshipAssertion had never had one. tools/test_semantic_carriers.py::CompositionCarrierTests fails the build if a bound class term goes missing again.",
      "Timestamp sweep: every property the CUE annotates with an XSD datatype now carries that datatype here. Ten temporal terms did not — rkaf:attestedAt, rkaf:revokedAt, rkaf:adoptedAt, rkaf:openedAt, rkaf:closedAt, rkaf:declaredAt, rkaf:resolvedAt, rkaf:validatedAt, rkaf:retroactiveFrom, rkaf:sunsetAt — so an attestation time expanded to a plain string while rkaf:assertedAt expanded to xsd:dateTime. rkaf:rationale joins them as xsd:string. tools/test_semantic_carriers.py::TypedValueCarrierTests fails the build if an annotated term loses its coercion again."
    ],
    "note": "_meta is JSON-LD-safe: keys not in @context are ignored by JSON-LD processors."
  }
}
